Package: sediros-audit
Version: 0.3.0
Architecture: @SEDIROS_ARCH@
Maintainer: The SedirOS Authors <ahmetatakan.tech@gmail.com>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: libc6, sediros-hardening, dpkg, iproute2, util-linux, mount, kmod, nftables, ufw, apt, systemd
Recommends: curl
Description: Check that a SedirOS system's hardening is still in place
 sediros-audit compares the running system with the hardening of the
 installed SedirOS packages: kernel settings, SSH, firewall, AppArmor,
 setuid programs, accounts, sudo, PAM, kernel modules, automatic updates,
 the SedirOS apt repository, boot settings, disk encryption and Secure Boot.
 It reports what was changed and, where it can, which file changed it.
 .
 Run: sudo sediros-audit   (--json for tools, --quiet for problems only)
 .
 It also runs daily (sediros-audit.timer): the result is shown at login,
 written as Prometheus metrics, and reported by e-mail or webhook when the
 hardening got worse (/etc/sediros/audit.conf).
